1
00:00:03,360 --> 00:00:04,990
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,430 --> 00:00:10,920
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:14,600
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:17,540
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,910 --> 00:00:21,640
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:27,080 --> 00:00:28,380
Not my choice...

7
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:30,510
I was not...

8
00:00:32,690 --> 00:00:35,050
I was not born as a woman by choice!

9
00:00:36,890 --> 00:00:42,390
What I can't forgive is how your
selfishness nearly got Griffith killed!

10
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:46,040
I don't care if you drop dead
somewhere in battle!

11
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:51,360
But I'll never forgive you if you ruin the
Band of the Hawk, Griffith's dream!

12
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:57,070
And I can't forgive you for
making Griffith change like he has...

13
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:04,110
Why?

14
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:08,930
Why did he choose you?

15
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:10,700
Why you?

16
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:33,530
Feel no shame about shape

17
00:01:33,610 --> 00:01:35,440
Weather changes their phrase

18
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:39,200
Even mother will show you another way

19
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,580
So put your glasses on

20
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:43,660
Nothing will be wrong

21
00:01:43,740 --> 00:01:45,870
There's no blame. There's no fame

22
00:01:45,870 --> 00:01:47,710
It's up to you

23
00:01:47,870 --> 00:01:51,340
The first words should be found

24
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:54,960
Whatever holds you back

25
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:56,340
I...

26
00:01:56,720 --> 00:01:57,470
...can...

27
00:01:57,550 --> 00:01:59,640
I can get it off

28
00:01:59,640 --> 00:02:00,640
Tell me what...

29
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:01,640
Tell me what...

30
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:03,470
Tell me what you want

31
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:04,560
I don't know why...

32
00:02:04,770 --> 00:02:05,560
Don't know why...

33
00:02:05,560 --> 00:02:07,560
Don't know why you're afraid

34
00:02:07,730 --> 00:02:08,730
Tell me what...

35
00:02:08,810 --> 00:02:09,690
Tell me what...

36
00:02:09,850 --> 00:02:11,360
Tell me what you'd say

37
00:02:11,610 --> 00:02:12,690
I don't know why...

38
00:02:12,820 --> 00:02:13,770
Don't know why...

39
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:14,570
Too late...

40
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:16,190
It's too late

41
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:25,120
Prepared for Death

42
00:03:33,150 --> 00:03:34,480
What's the matter?

43
00:03:34,480 --> 00:03:35,360
Are you giving up?

44
00:03:39,150 --> 00:03:42,990
Oh brother, a woman
can be such a nuisance.

45
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:48,040
A woman has no strength. She can
lose her temper at the drop of a hat.

46
00:03:48,370 --> 00:03:50,160
Not only that, but you're on your period.

47
00:03:51,210 --> 00:03:54,540
At any rate, women just aren't cut out for war.

48
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:57,340
You know nothing about women!

49
00:03:57,340 --> 00:03:59,510
Of course not. I'm a man, so how could I know?

50
00:04:00,840 --> 00:04:04,720
What I do know is that
we don't have the time...

51
00:04:04,720 --> 00:04:08,180
...to be stranded here
by your woman problems any longer.

52
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:13,020
The enemy doesn't care about your
condition or if you are a woman or not.

53
00:04:13,690 --> 00:04:16,860
On second thought...
they are probably glad, wouldn't you say?

54
00:04:26,450 --> 00:04:27,370
Let's move!

55
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:23,420
What the hell?

56
00:05:54,750 --> 00:05:58,370
Hey, is this a breeding ground
for swarms of mosquitoes?

57
00:06:00,540 --> 00:06:02,210
I found you.

58
00:06:05,210 --> 00:06:08,300
I am glad you are alive, kid!

59
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:12,140
Hey, old man,
you're looking pretty good yourself.

60
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:12,760
Shut up!

61
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:18,770
Even though it was a fluke, a bastard
like you caused me some real trouble.

62
00:06:18,770 --> 00:06:22,940
I, a proud Tudor knight, could not bear
to die without rectifying the situation!

63
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:23,940
Oh, really?

64
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:26,530
I'm not going to let you die easily.

65
00:06:26,530 --> 00:06:31,280
I will haul you off as a captive
and expose you to hell on earth.

66
00:06:31,280 --> 00:06:34,870
You'll enjoy a secret torture technique,
the 100-year Monzetsu Goroshi...

67
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:38,120
...that has been passed down through
the Coborlwitz family for 200 years!

68
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:40,420
I didn't think you'd still be holding a grudge.

69
00:06:40,750 --> 00:06:43,210
If you surrender without protest, I'll spare you.

70
00:06:43,210 --> 00:06:44,460
But if you want to cross us...

71
00:06:44,460 --> 00:06:47,380
...we'll chop off your arms along
with any other body parts we like!

72
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:49,970
So long as you're alive, it does not matter.

73
00:06:50,430 --> 00:06:55,140
As for the woman, we will make her
a plaything for my soldiers right here!

74
00:06:55,930 --> 00:06:58,390
I have to suggest that you don't try that.

75
00:07:00,190 --> 00:07:01,940
She is a truly scary woman.

76
00:07:02,690 --> 00:07:04,360
She'll rip you to shreds.

77
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:09,320
How dare you joke around with me!

78
00:07:09,610 --> 00:07:10,860
Beat them down!

79
00:07:49,110 --> 00:07:52,240
I don't need your help anymore!

80
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:54,410
Great!

81
00:07:54,410 --> 00:07:55,490
Damn!

82
00:07:55,490 --> 00:07:57,120
There are only two of them!

83
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:57,870
Don't hesitate!

84
00:07:58,450 --> 00:08:00,450
Overwhelm them in a single charge!

85
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:58,140
They are incompetents, every one of them.

86
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,640
Samson!

87
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:01,930
Samson!

88
00:09:01,930 --> 00:09:04,600
Here, Big Brother!

89
00:09:17,530 --> 00:09:21,450
Assistant commander of the Blue
Whale Heavy Assault Knights...

90
00:09:21,450 --> 00:09:22,450
Samson!

91
00:09:24,870 --> 00:09:28,460
He is my younger brother and second
strongest warrior in my entire unit!

92
00:09:28,460 --> 00:09:32,880
Additionally, Samson's armor is three
times as thick as anyone else's!

93
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:35,840
Even buried under an avalanche,
he would be absolutely indestructible!

94
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:44,930
On top of that, his iron ball can crush
a buffalo's head flat in a single blow!

95
00:09:45,230 --> 00:09:48,730
If a man gets hit squarely by it,
nothing will remain but a piece of flesh!

96
00:09:49,650 --> 00:09:51,360
Now, I give you no quarter!

97
00:09:51,860 --> 00:09:53,360
Have them experience firsthand...

98
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:55,240
...the esteemed techniques
of the Coborlwitz family!

99
00:10:01,990 --> 00:10:04,330
A sword would be smashed
if used to block his attacks directly.

100
00:10:08,620 --> 00:10:09,670
What should we do?

101
00:10:26,430 --> 00:10:27,770
He knocked it back?

102
00:10:35,570 --> 00:10:37,150
I can't believe it...

103
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:40,990
He's beating back every blow
from Samson's iron ball...

104
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:45,370
Oh, I see!

105
00:10:45,370 --> 00:10:48,620
He has no time to dodge the blows
because of their incredible speed!

106
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:50,080
No...

107
00:10:50,080 --> 00:10:51,380
With Guts's skill...

108
00:10:51,380 --> 00:10:53,790
...he should be able to evade and attack.

109
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:57,260
There's no need for him
to damage his sword like that...

110
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:05,260
He's protecting me...

111
00:11:14,310 --> 00:11:15,360
He's injured...

112
00:11:16,860 --> 00:11:19,280
The arrow wound I inflicted upon you when...

113
00:11:19,280 --> 00:11:22,360
...you were trying to protect that
woman seems to be bothering you!

114
00:11:23,530 --> 00:11:24,990
Quit your dawdling!

115
00:11:24,990 --> 00:11:26,240
He's been injured!

116
00:11:26,240 --> 00:11:27,950
Finish him off quickly!

117
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:29,620
Hey!

118
00:11:30,660 --> 00:11:32,830
I'll clear the way for you...

119
00:11:32,830 --> 00:11:36,090
...and then you sprint for the woods.

120
00:11:36,590 --> 00:11:37,170
But...

121
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:46,560
What the...

122
00:12:12,870 --> 00:12:14,750
S-Samson...

123
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:15,960
Now!

124
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:17,040
Get away from here!

125
00:12:17,380 --> 00:12:18,880
Get your ass moving!

126
00:12:18,880 --> 00:12:19,710
Run!

127
00:12:20,170 --> 00:12:21,050
But...

128
00:12:21,050 --> 00:12:22,220
What are you doing?

129
00:12:22,220 --> 00:12:23,010
Go right now!

130
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:24,470
No way...

131
00:12:24,890 --> 00:12:26,180
I just can't...

132
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:29,140
I won't leave without you!

133
00:12:31,310 --> 00:12:32,430
Shoot!

134
00:12:32,430 --> 00:12:34,350
Aim for the woman and kill her off!

135
00:12:42,240 --> 00:12:43,200
Foolish!

136
00:12:43,650 --> 00:12:47,660
You repeatedly get wounded
on behalf of a mere woman.

137
00:12:48,330 --> 00:12:50,790
How stupid you are!

138
00:12:54,330 --> 00:12:55,370
Why?

139
00:12:55,670 --> 00:12:57,380
Don't get the wrong idea.

140
00:12:58,500 --> 00:13:02,260
A sickly person is of no use
here, so I want you to get lost.

141
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:05,220
It's not my nature to evade the enemy.

142
00:13:06,090 --> 00:13:10,720
Besides, I've got to get even
with that sniveling bastard.

143
00:13:12,270 --> 00:13:18,810
As you said, maybe
I'm content just wielding my sword...

144
00:13:20,150 --> 00:13:22,480
But you're different, right?

145
00:13:24,530 --> 00:13:27,820
Do you want to die in a place like this?

146
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:32,700
Do you want to die a meaningless
death in this little skirmish?

147
00:13:33,620 --> 00:13:37,290
Has the wish you hold in
your heart rotted away that much?

148
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:42,300
There are times when
a sword needs to be sheathed.

149
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:47,430
Go back to the sheath that protects you.

150
00:13:49,550 --> 00:13:51,640
Go back to Griffith.

151
00:14:04,070 --> 00:14:07,360
Go back to the sheath that protects you.

152
00:14:08,240 --> 00:14:10,490
Go back to Griffith.

153
00:14:40,350 --> 00:14:41,690
Hurry up!

154
00:14:41,690 --> 00:14:42,190
Run!

155
00:14:43,570 --> 00:14:44,520
Go!

156
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:45,690
Get out of here!

157
00:14:49,490 --> 00:14:51,870
I promise to return with our comrades!

158
00:14:51,870 --> 00:14:53,120
Don't die until then!

159
00:14:57,950 --> 00:14:59,500
Don't let her get away!

160
00:14:59,500 --> 00:15:01,080
Get her and kill her off!

161
00:15:03,290 --> 00:15:07,090
You shouldn't go chasing after
women until you get your work done...

162
00:15:07,090 --> 00:15:08,550
...you scheming cowards!

163
00:15:08,550 --> 00:15:10,300
You bastard!

164
00:15:19,230 --> 00:15:20,980
W-What a man!

165
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:24,110
He beats armored men as if
they were cherries to be picked.

166
00:15:24,110 --> 00:15:27,530
It's unbelievable, but a man drops
every time he swings his sword!

167
00:15:27,980 --> 00:15:31,150
I didn't know that such a man
existed among the enemy lines.

168
00:15:33,490 --> 00:15:37,370
My sword is blunt.
The blade has gotten dull.

169
00:15:37,830 --> 00:15:42,120
However, it's three times as thick and
three times as heavy as any other.

170
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:45,960
Just hope you die when I hit you,
or you'll be in lots of pain.

171
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:49,760
You son of a bitch!

172
00:15:50,260 --> 00:15:51,050
Look here!

173
00:15:51,510 --> 00:15:53,550
All of you, stop dawdling!

174
00:15:53,550 --> 00:15:56,970
Though he is skilled, the enemy
is only one wounded man!

175
00:15:57,310 --> 00:15:59,930
All we have to do is
surround him, and he'll be finished!

176
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:02,310
We number one hundred men!

177
00:16:02,310 --> 00:16:03,230
Get him!

178
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:05,360
Don't talk nonsense.

179
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:08,320
Is there anyone who wants
to take revenge for Samson?

180
00:16:08,650 --> 00:16:09,940
No one wants to.

181
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:13,150
Are you all really proud knights of Tudor?

182
00:16:13,150 --> 00:16:14,910
Actually, we're mercenaries over here.

183
00:16:18,120 --> 00:16:22,410
I will pay triple the reward
I promised if someone beheads him...

184
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:26,630
No, wait. I'll even increase the amount by five...

185
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:31,970
And I'll guarantee your promotion
to battalion commander!

186
00:16:31,970 --> 00:16:33,930
F-Five times the reward...

187
00:16:33,930 --> 00:16:35,390
What should we do?

188
00:16:35,390 --> 00:16:37,640
Naturally, we've got to give it a shot.

189
00:16:38,140 --> 00:16:41,430
It looks like he can't move around
too much with that wound.

190
00:16:41,430 --> 00:16:43,980
It'll be possible if we get a group
of five men or so to challenge him.

191
00:16:45,690 --> 00:16:47,650
What are you bitching about?

192
00:16:48,270 --> 00:16:49,610
I'm leaving then.

193
00:16:51,360 --> 00:16:54,700
That's right.
That's how mercenaries have to be.

194
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:55,490
Right?

195
00:17:14,970 --> 00:17:15,590
Pursuers?

196
00:17:16,550 --> 00:17:17,390
Four...

197
00:17:17,720 --> 00:17:19,220
No, there are five...

198
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:39,570
Die!

199
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:49,290
Pull yourself together!

200
00:17:49,290 --> 00:17:51,210
Damn it, that bitch...

201
00:17:51,210 --> 00:17:52,800
Get her!

202
00:18:11,820 --> 00:18:13,190
What are you doing?

203
00:18:13,190 --> 00:18:14,820
Kill him at once!

204
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:27,370
We did it!

205
00:18:32,920 --> 00:18:33,800
Good!

206
00:18:33,800 --> 00:18:36,510
We've crippled his left hand now!

207
00:18:37,510 --> 00:18:42,300
He won't be able to wield
his huge sword so easily.

208
00:18:42,300 --> 00:18:43,680
Beat him!

209
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:50,310
Now it's getting interesting.

210
00:19:24,350 --> 00:19:25,720
This is the end...

211
00:19:26,060 --> 00:19:27,640
I can't run anymore...

212
00:19:49,370 --> 00:19:51,710
Oopsie, I bet you'd like to get your hands on that.

213
00:19:51,710 --> 00:19:55,590
You put us through a lot of trouble, girl.

214
00:19:59,590 --> 00:20:03,260
We can put you out of
your misery soon, but...

215
00:20:04,220 --> 00:20:09,020
A whole bunch of my comrades
were killed by you, so...

216
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:12,730
Before killing you off,
I've got to thank you for that.

217
00:20:28,080 --> 00:20:30,790
Don't glower at me like that.

218
00:20:30,790 --> 00:20:36,250
I'm offering you all the fun you want
right before setting out for the afterlife.

219
00:20:36,710 --> 00:20:39,500
You should show me some gratitude.

220
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:44,180
Well, well...

221
00:20:56,520 --> 00:20:59,020
What's wrong?
Are you embarrassed?

222
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:02,570
I don't care if you command
a thousand men in battle or not...

223
00:21:02,940 --> 00:21:06,450
Now look at you. You don't seem
to have any authority over me at all.

224
00:21:13,410 --> 00:21:16,170
I'm unable to push this bastard aside...

225
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:18,000
Why...

226
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,420
Why is my arm so powerless...

227
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

228
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

229
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

230
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

231
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

232
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

233
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

234
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

235
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

236
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

237
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

